       Displays properties for the given datasets.  If no datasets are speci‐
       fied, then the command displays properties for all datasets on the sys‐
       tem.  For each property, the following columns are displayed:
           nnaammee      Dataset name
           pprrooppeerrttyy  Property name
           vvaalluuee     Property value
           ssoouurrccee    Property source llooccaall, ddeeffaauulltt, iinnhheerriitteedd, tteemmppoorraarryy,
                     rreecceeiivveedd, or -- (none).

       All columns are displayed by default, though this can be controlled by
       using the --oo option.  This command takes a comma-separated list of
       properties as described in the _N_a_t_i_v_e _P_r_o_p_e_r_t_i_e_s and _U_s_e_r _P_r_o_p_e_r_t_i_e_s
       sections of zfsprops(7).

       The value aallll can be used to display all properties that apply to the
       given dataset's type (ffiilleessyysstteemm, vvoolluummee, ssnnaappsshhoott, or bbooookkmmaarrkk).

       --HH         Display output in a form more easily parsed by scripts.  Any
                  headers are omitted, and fields are explicitly separated by
                  a single tab instead of an arbitrary amount of space.

       --dd _d_e_p_t_h   Recursively display any children of the dataset, limiting
                  the recursion to _d_e_p_t_h.  A depth of 11 will display only the
                  dataset and its direct children.

       --oo _f_i_e_l_d   A comma-separated list of columns to display, defaults to
                  nnaammee,pprrooppeerrttyy,vvaalluuee,ssoouurrccee.

       --pp         Display numbers in parsable (exact) values.

       --rr         Recursively display properties for any children.

       --ss _s_o_u_r_c_e  A comma-separated list of sources to display.  Those proper‐
                  ties coming from a source other than those in this list are
                  ignored.  Each source must be one of the following: llooccaall,
                  ddeeffaauulltt, iinnhheerriitteedd, tteemmppoorraarryy, rreecceeiivveedd, or nnoonnee.  The de‐
                  fault value is all sources.

       --tt _t_y_p_e    A comma-separated list of types to display, where _t_y_p_e is
                  one of ffiilleessyysstteemm, ssnnaappsshhoott, vvoolluummee, bbooookkmmaarrkk, or aallll.

